            <ArticleTitle>Neutropenia occurring after starting gabapentin for neuropathic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>575-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of neutropenia occurring in a patient receiving gabapentin for neuropathic pain. Five weeks after treatment started, the patient was admitted to hospital with neutropenic sepsis. Gabapentin is widely used, and neutropenia is a rare adverse effect. This case highlights a serious and potential life-threatening complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
